<!--Post: 3246--><!--Time: 1104668932-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3246"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Skov<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Skov<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 02, 2005 - 4:28 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Here is a link to the woman who states that she was a friend of Josephine Otero, posting on AMW. <BR> <BR> <BR><a href="http://forums.prospero.com/foxamw/messages?msg=489.28" target=_top>http://forums.prospero.com/foxamw/messages?msg=489 .28</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3246-->
<!--Post: 3255--><!--Time: 1104695396-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3255"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Cyndi<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Cyndi<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 02, 2005 - 11:49 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->WhoisBTK, I would like to address #3 of your proposed scenario.  If the two &#34;Osborne&#34; children could possibly identify BTK then why would he not wait and kill the remaining children when they arrived home from school?  If &#34;he&#34; possibly lived nearby or visited infrequently couldn&#39;t the other children identify him also?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3255-->
<!--Post: 3261--><!--Time: 1104703296-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3261"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->J<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->J<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 02, 2005 - 2:01 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Q: <BR>Yes, tornado drill makes more sense for that part of the country AND that particular time. I found a web site listing the tornado history of KS and there were apparently 2 tornadoes hitting Sedgwick County in October &#39;73.  One of these injured 15 people, less than three months prior to the murders.  A key thing we&#39;re told when tornadoes approach - get into a closet in the middle of the house.  Perhaps the Otero parents had drills and Charlie&#39;s memory filling may have incorporated hiding in the closet in/around that time of his life. <BR> <BR>Back to the issue of the profile: <BR>I don&#39;t buy the notion of drug-dealing.  It seems to me the MO indicates a planned killing for the &#34;fun&#34; of it &#40;pardon me for saying it that way&#41;, whereas I suspect drug-related killing is more direct and quick &#40;walk in and shoot - not necessarily torture and ejaculate&#41;.  Mike, is this not true? <BR> <BR>Also, my guess has always been : a&#41; he may have had some killing experience prior to the Oteros &#40;maybe via war-related killing&#41;; b&#41; he knew at least one member of the Otero family and maybe some negative relationship made these people be selected as his &#34;debut&#34; into public killing; c&#41; now that he had these killings accomplished, the drive took hold and he went about planning the other killings, typically selecting young, lone, white thin light-colored hair victims.  If you&#39;ll notice the photos on this web site, Bright, Fox, and Wegerle have similar features.  I suspect Vian was a last minute plan; she didn&#39;t appear to be thin and particularly pretty.  Perhaps the photo he showed to the Vian child was of the INTENDED victim&#40;s&#41;, not Vian &#40;do we know?&#41; and when he failed to find them, he went with Vian instead. <BR> <BR>Mike: does this fit with your profile?  Do Sks follow a pattern like that: first major kill is of known victims, based on some personal issues, then a pattern of selecting unknown victims who share similar features? <BR> <BR>&#40;And, on this note....I&#39;ve not taken the time to read up on all of the possible victims. Do any of them fit the young, thin, blond pattern?&#41;<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3261-->
<!--Post: 3279--><!--Time: 1104727452-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3279"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Mike_kelleher<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Mike_kelleher<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 02, 2005 - 8:44 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->J: <BR> <BR>I do not see any evidence of a drug-related crime with any of BTK&#39;s activities. However, I do believe that BTK was familiar with the Otero family, or at least one member &#40;as you said&#41;. I would not put much stock in &#34;look alike&#34; victims in this case, simply because of the multiple murder aspect and the way the murders were carried out. It is possible but I wouldn&#39;t rate it highly likely. It is more likely that he knew each of the victims, although in a more passing way than the Oteros. I use the term &#34;knew&#34; here is a very loose sense, as in at least having seen the victims on several occasions before the attacks. I rather doubt that any of the murders were &#34;last minute.&#34; In fact, BTK was prepared, selected his victims, and planned accordingly. He was, to use an outdated way of thinking, an &#34;organized&#34; killer. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3279-->
<!--Post: 3281--><!--Time: 1104732990-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3281"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->J<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->J<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 02, 2005 - 10:16 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Mike: thanks so much for your quick response to my questions. <BR> <BR>I thought there were indeed cases where SKs choose look-alikes.  No?   <BR> <BR>The only mutliple event was the Oteros, right?  Wasn&#39;t Kevin Bright assumed to be unanticipated? <BR> <BR>By &#34;last minute&#34; on Vian, I meant to suggest a last minute &#42;switch&#42;.  IF the photo he showed to the kid was of someone he INTENDED to find &#40;not Vian&#41;, but the kid didn&#39;t give helpful info or BTK failed to locate the person....then maybe he switched to Vian instead &#40;since he was all prepared to kill that day&#41;.  This is just a thought and one that helps put Vian in a slightly separate category than Bright, Fox, Wegerle, and perhaps any additional possible victims yet to be linked.  Only BTK knows for sure, of course. <BR> <BR>I understand what you&#39;re saying about &#34;knowing&#34; the victims in a loose sense...perhaps via watching them from a distance, etc.  This still qualifies as &#34;unknown&#34; in my general definition &#40;i.e., BTK was unknown to them at least; no meaningful relationship existed between them.&#41; <BR> <BR>Thanks again for your response.  I admire your work and willingness to share your thoughts with us.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3281-->
<!--Post: 3287--><!--Time: 1104740126-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3287"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Whoisbtk<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Whoisbtk<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 03, 2005 - 12:15 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Mike_Kelleher <BR>J <BR>     I don&#39;t like drug dealing as the underlying issue either.  I think your idea of prior military related homicides is much better. But I think I think some issue/reason has to be present in some form because: <BR> <BR>&#42;IF&#42; Charlie is accurate about the fear, closet, etc. <BR> <BR>&#42;THEN&#42; there is a reason BTK threatens Mr. Osborne, and <BR> <BR>&#42;THEN&#42; there is a reason why Mr. Osborne won&#39;t ask police or adult friends for help.   <BR> <BR>We don&#39;t have to know what these reasons were for this hypothesis to function, but clearly this area of the hypothesis needs firming up. <BR> <BR>If anyone has suggestions about what these prior crime/event/reasons might be, please jump in. <BR> <BR> <BR>Cyndi: Those are good questions.  My thinking on your points, plus one more: <BR> <BR>Here’s One More:  We have assumed that BTK knew two of the five children remained at home, what if he didn’t.  He was surveilling the house most likely from a distance, the routine was Mr. Osborne taking all the children, BTK would have seen the children and Mr.Osborne get in and leave.  If he wasn’t counting, he might think they were following their routine and all five children were gone. <BR>He doesn’t think anyone is there but Mrs. Osborne until he pushes his way in. <BR> <BR> <BR>1.  Why didn&#39;t he wait for the other children to come home?  Because two children had gone to school, and lunchtime becomes a problem because: <BR> <BR>     a.  Photos show considerable snow, if the children at school are expecting to come home for lunch, and there&#39;s no ride, they call and there&#39;s no answer &#40;I don&#39;t know what it sounds like to call a phone that’s been cut&#41; but someone at school could report trouble on the line and repairmen show up.  A child at school with a missing ride can be an issue.   <BR> <BR>     b.  BTK could not be sure the children wouldn&#39;t get a ride home at noon from a teacher or another parent, or that they wouldn&#39;t come home with a friend for lunch.  Same for after school. <BR> <BR>     c. One or all three might stay after school, or go to a friend’s house, etc. <BR> <BR>This could explain why he didn&#39;t wait for the remaining children: it&#39;s too unpredictable in terms of how long he waits, what if they get a ride from a concerned teacher who waits in a their car in the driveway for an &#34;OK&#34;.  <BR> <BR>[This would also set a time frame on the killing: he had to be done long enough before noon that he&#39;s gone before there&#39;s any risk of the children coming home for lunch.  This fits the reported time of death as “sometime before noon” ”<a href="http://www.kansas.com/mld/kansas/news/special_packages/btk/history/8312877.htm" target=_top>http://www.kansas.com/mld/kansas/news/special_pack ages/btk/history/8312877.htm</a>] <BR> <BR>2.  Why didn&#39;t the surviving children identify BTK, or put another way, if the two children in the house knew who BTK was why didn&#39;t the surviving children know also? <BR> <BR>     a.  All the children may have known who he was, but only the two at home have the specialized knowledge that he is the killer. <BR> <BR>     b.  The two children who went to school lack this specialized knowledge.  They might have known him, but not being there they could not link him to the killing of their parents.  At best they could only identify him as one of hundreds of people their parents knew.  This explains why the two at home are killed as witnesses, even though their siblings couldn&#39;t identify the killer <BR> <BR>     c.  Immediately afterwards the children were taken into protective custody by SRS &#40;a child welfare agency&#41; and ultimately placed with family friends in New Mexico.  He couldn&#39;t find them. <BR> <BR>     d.  Also it would have soon been obvious to BTK that neither surviving child had given the police a &#34;smoking gun&#34; suspect, and the need to pursue them would diminish. <BR> <BR>     e.  If the secret relationship between BTK and Mr. Osborne were so awful that he couldn&#39;t tell police, it wouldn&#39;t be unusual for a father to have concealed this kind of secret from his children. <BR> <BR> <BR>Skoal and J <BR> <BR>Thanks for the questions and critique [I tend to fall in love with my own theories; reality checks are always welcome] <BR> <BR>Good points on the MO.  Is it possible, though, that BTK may have combined business and pleasure; in other words, if he was going to kill anyway enjoying the act is a bonus. <BR> <BR>Or, he may have learned to like it in this event, he may have been unaware of his tendencies until this killing, Mike_Kelleher could speak to that better. <BR> <BR>Again please don’t get hung up on the drug issue, there’s no evidence of &#42;any&#42; criminal activity by any Otero.  All I’m saying is that Charlie Otero’s statement raises two &#42; red flags&#42;: 1&#41; why did BTK want to hurt the Otero’s, and 2&#41; knowing of the threat why didn’t Mr. Otero call police? <BR> <BR> <BR>I&#39;m proposing this hypothesis to test the assumption that C.O. was accurately reporting his father&#39;s awareness of a serious threat to his family rather than dismissing it out-of-hand because it doesn&#39;t fit a given theory of profile.  Any plausible theory/profile must account for &#42;all&#42; of the evidence, not just some of it. <BR> <BR>I remain concerned about a procrustean analytical process that rejects facts and evidence because they don&#39;t fit someone&#39;s theory,  “Procruste’s Bed” &#40;<a href="http://www.bartleby.com/81/13673.html" target=_top>http://www.bartleby.com/81/13673.html</a>&#41;. <BR> <BR> <BR><a href="mailto:whoisbtk@yahoo.com">whoisbtk@yahoo.com</a> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3287-->
<!--Post: 3289--><!--Time: 1104741242-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3289"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Q<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Q<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 03, 2005 - 12:34 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Whoisbtk, <BR> <BR>You wrote: &#34;I&#39;m proposing this hypothesis to test the assumption that C.O. was accurately reporting his father&#39;s awareness of a serious threat to his family&#34; <BR> <BR>If this is the case, as C.O. asserted &#40;when did he say this...back in the 70&#39;s or more recent?&#41; then why would Mr. Otero leave his two children and wife alone? <BR> <BR>1. He thought the trip to be a short one and in daytime? <BR> <BR>2. I read that the family were all Judo students but then why hide them in a closet? <BR> <BR>3. He thought the threat had passed or wouldn&#39;t or couldn&#39;t happen at that time of day, day of the week? <BR> <BR>4. He was mislead to believe the threat had passed or wouldn&#39;t happen purposly by BTK because they had a close relashionship of some kind either including his wife or not... professional? <BR> <BR> Something else?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3289-->
<!--Post: 3306--><!--Time: 1104774302-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3306"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Armchairpi<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Armchairpi<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 03, 2005 - 9:45 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Dr. Kelleher- <BR> <BR>I hope to see your comments regarding Zodiac and BTK one day soon.  As a reader of <i>This is the Zodiac Speaking</i>, I understand you to believe the murderer of Cheri Jo Bates to _not_ be the Zodiac, but someone known to the Zodiac &#40;a boyhood friend, perhaps&#41;.  Is this correct?  A very farfetched theory discussed on this message board involved a &#34;suspect&#34; who originated from the general Riverside, CA area, and it reminded me of this theory of yours....  I believe Tom has expunged references to this &#34;suspect&#34; from the board. <BR> <BR>I think it&#39;s glaring to those familiar with both cases that BTK has not only a fascination with the Zodiac, but seems to want to link himself to the Zodiac in some way; to intertwine their crimes by &#34;copying&#34; language from letters, details of crimes, etc..  I hope in your comments regarding BTK and Zodiac you might include some insight into this.  Why does BTK seem to have a fascination with the Zodiac?  Why the Zodiac in particular &#40;instead of Bundy, or Gein, for examples&#41;? Why does BTK feel compelled to muddy his crimes with the crimes of the Zodiac?  What conclusions can be drawn about BTK&#39;s underlying psychology from these facts, and what clues as to BTK&#39;s daily life might these facts provide &#40;for instance, you have said that we should expect BTK to be monitoring and participating in internet discussion of his own case- might we also expect him to be interacting at _Zodiac_ crime websites or with other Zodiac crime buffs via the internet?&#41;?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3306-->
<!--Post: 3307--><!--Time: 1104775331-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3307"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Armchairpi<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Armchairpi<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 03, 2005 - 10:02 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Dr. Kelleher- <BR> <BR>P.S. On a reread of my post, I realize I might have been too obtuse in my first thought: I wonder if you suspect BTK might have more than a &#34;purely intellectual/psychological&#34; connection to the Zodiac.  For example, would your investigative BTK profile include to look for a suspect&#39;s connection during the 1960&#39;s or 70&#39;s to Vallejo, San Francisco, Napa, or Riverside, CA?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3307-->
<!--Post: 3308--><!--Time: 1104775704-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3308"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Mike_kelleher<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Mike_kelleher<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 03, 2005 - 10:08 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I&#39;m not sure about the BTK/Zodiac connection. BTK does show an &#34;interest&#34; in Zodiac methodology but it&#39;s hard to say if there is any more to it. Zodiac was a very unique killer and an obvious master of manipulating the media. From that point of view, others may want to emulate his behavior and get the attention he got. If there&#39;s more to it than this aspect, I haven&#39;t seen any proof.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3308-->
<!--Post: 3322--><!--Time: 1104800087-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3322"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Armchairpi<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Armchairpi<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 03, 2005 - 4:54 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I&#39;m guessing you believe the writing to the police and press, the phone calls, and the selection/announcement of a scary moniker and symbol fall into the category of &#34;showing an interest in Zodiac methodology&#34;. <BR> <BR>But, I&#39;m also referring to some other items that have been discussed in a couple or three well marked threads regarding BTK &amp; Zodiac.  Ones that come to mind are: <BR> <BR>1&#41;leaving behind a single clear print at one of the crime scenes while at the same time seeming to be so meticulous in general not to leave prints &#40;some speculate this is an homage to the Zodiac-Stine cab prints&#41;; <BR> <BR>2&#41; at least one turn of a Zodiac phrase &#40;&#34;Will there be more?&#34;&#41; in police-corrborated BTK correspondence, and other phrases from poster&#40;s&#41; on the message board suspected by some to be BTK; <BR> <BR>3&#41; a possible &#34;Riverside&#34;/&#34;Indian Hills&#34; correlation between Cheri Jo Bates and Vicki Wegerle &#40;if I understand correctly, V.W. is the only major suspected BTK victim to be outside of an otherwise tight radius and lived in &#34;Indian Hills&#34;, which is extremely close to an area of Wichita known as &#34;Riverside&#34;; while CJB lived in Riverside, which has an &#34;Indian Hills&#34; very nearby it&#41;; <BR> <BR>4&#41; as Tom pointed out, a striking similarity in the way the Bright attack was committed in comparison to Berryessa &#40;I might add to what Tom said that, if I&#39;m not mistaken, in both attacks the woman died, while the man survived, &#42;and&#42; in both the perp made idle chit chat: &#34;escaped from Montana penitentiary&#34; and &#34;haven&#39;t I seen you at the university?&#34;&#41;; <BR> <BR>5&#41; a plea by BTK for more press coverage &#40;much like Z&#39;s demands for column inches and Zodiac buttons, etc.&#41;, while oddly leaving the Zodiac &#42;out&#42; of a long list of serial killers who got a lot of press; <BR> <BR>6&#41; many correlations between Zodiac/BTK dates and numerology. <BR> <BR>You&#39;re right- not &#34;proof&#34;, but do you think these coincidences are suspicious and might have implications on a BTK profile?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3322-->
<!--Post: 3365--><!--Time: 1104826345-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3365"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Oklahoma_mike<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Oklahoma_mike<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 04, 2005 - 12:12 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->See my upcoming post regarding some of these issues in the Victims-Oteros thread.  We get a bit far afield here at times,<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3365-->
<!--Post: 3385--><!--Time: 1104860418-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3385"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Whoisbtk<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Whoisbtk<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 04, 2005 - 9:40 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Q <BR>Good questions <BR> <BR>1. Charlie Otero said this in a phone interview with an AP reporter, Roxana Hegeman, either 11/30/2004 or 12/1/2004.  The story ran in the Dodge City Daily Globe on December 1, 2004 &#40;<a href="http://dodgeglobe.com/stories/120104/state_120104008.shtml" target=_top>http://dodgeglobe.com/stories/120104/state_1201040 08.shtml</a>&#41; <BR>  <BR>My vote for most likely is #1, a short trip in daylight. Here are the route, distances, and times: <BR> <BR>Edgemoor to 2nd street &#40;1/2mi.&#41; to Oliver &#40;1/2mi.&#41;, drop the children off on the school side of Oliver. Then Oliver to Central &#40;1/4mi.&#41; to Edgemoor &#40;1/2mi.&#41;To 803 Edgemoor &#40;1/4mi.&#41; The distance is 2 miles with 4 traffic lights and one 20mph school zone.  Even on icy roads, getting stuck at all the signals and stopped in the school zone, a 20mph average makes a 6min. trip.  Add 5 min. for signals and school zones; it&#39;s a 10-12 min. trip.  [Mapquest has the round trip as 1.96 miles, 6 min. drive time] <BR> <BR>Bottom line, it&#39;s about a 10 min trip. <BR> <BR>So it&#39;s short, in daylight, and the alternative is have the children get to school themselves, but: <BR> <BR>a.  Wichita Public Schools will not bus students who live within 2 miles of school.  The Otero home was one mile from school and had no school bus, they would have walked, which is more dangerous for them if BTK is stalking the family. <BR> <BR>b. Even if danger to the children isn&#39;t a factor, the weather was probably too bad for walking a mile.  Photos of the Otero home taken later in the day show snow on the east side of the home and slush in the street.  The neighbor that called police was shoveling snow when the children came home from school.  This indicates cold weather and recent snowfall.  Living in Wichita I am aware that it would have been cold, windy, and icy that morning.  The children needed a ride because of the weather seems like the best explanation.   <BR> <BR>So, &#34; He thought the trip to be a short one and in daytime&#34; with the added factor of weather on a walk to school seems likely. <BR> <BR><a href="mailto:whoisbtk@yahoo.com">whoisbtk@yahoo.com</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3385-->
<!--Post: 3388--><!--Time: 1104861406-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3388"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Skov<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Skov<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 04, 2005 - 9:56 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hi Whoisbtk <BR> <BR>Here is what I found about the weather jan 15th 1974. <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.google.dk/search?q=cache:9H9A3cYrd98J:www.kansas.com/mld/kansas/news/special_packages/btk/archive/8348962.htm%2Bbtk%2B%2Bsun%2B%2Botero%2B%2Bsnow&amp;hl=en" target=_top>http://www.google.dk/search?q=cache:9H9A3cYrd98J:w ww.kansas.com/mld/kansas/news/special_packages/btk /archive/8348962.htm&#43;btk&#43;%2Bsun&#43;%2Botero&#43;%2Bsnow&amp;h l=en</a> <BR> <BR>In northeast Wichita, the sun was turning snow to slush when Charlie Otero returned home from Robinson Junior High School at 3:40 p.m.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3388-->
<!--Post: 3437--><!--Time: 1104896029-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3437"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Whoisbtk<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Whoisbtk<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 04, 2005 - 7:33 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Mike_kelleher <BR> <BR>Could we address the &#34;memory filling&#34; issue again, please? <BR> <BR>After the WPD release of details on 11/30/2004, Charlie Otero had a phone interview with an AP reporter from Dodge City, published 12/1/2004. [Link: <a href="http://dodgeglobe.com/stories/120104/state_1201040" target=_top>http://dodgeglobe.com/stories/120104/state_1201040</a> 08.shtml]  In this interview, he says he thought his father knew BTK.  In support, he recounts three specific events: <BR> <BR>1. Power went out in the house.  Mr. Otero made the family get in a closet and stay until he learned that power was out in the neighborhood. <BR> <BR>2.  A telephone repairman came to the house.  Mr. Otero wouldn&#39;t let him in until he saw a phone company truck. <BR> <BR>3.  Shortly before the murders, Mr. Otero tried to give Charlie his ring in case something should happen to him.  Charlie says he told his father that he &#40;the father&#41; would probably outlive him &#40;Charlie&#41;. <BR> <BR>Are these three specific recollections typical of &#34;memory filling&#34;? <BR> <BR>As a followup, if appropriate to this thread, why would Mr. Otero not call the police? <BR> <BR><a href="mailto:whoisbtk@yahoo.com">whoisbtk@yahoo.com</a>  <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3437-->
<!--Post: 3469--><!--Time: 1104946920-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3469"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Mike_kelleher<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Mike_kelleher<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 05, 2005 - 9:42 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->It&#39;s really impossible to say, one way or another. Why his father acted the way he did is interesting. But, we have no objective idea WHY he acted that way. Fears can be real, unreal, rational, irrational, specific, vague, founded or unfounded. Anyway, you get the picture. It&#39;s just too distant of a link for me to get overly excited about it.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3469-->
<!--Post: 3503--><!--Time: 1104970399-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3503"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Juno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Juno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 05, 2005 - 4:13 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Does anyone think that maybe the Oteros wer not the first?  I tend to think that Zodiac was responsible for the Santa Barbara beach murder prior to being &#34;the zodiac.&#34;  Then he just point blank shot two people in a car. <BR> <BR>I would think that something like the Otero murders was a bit much for a first time, especially in such a &#34;hands-on&#34; fashion and that he probably started with one victim. <BR> <BR>I don&#39;t know where else to put this thought, so I will add it here.  There was some discussion about mentioning other killers in the letter.  I think he felt a sort of kinship with them, a sense of belonging.  I beleive he read as much about them as possible and learned from them.  A sick sort of mentorship.  I beleive he is identifies most with glatman, although the mystique and media savvy of Zodiac is certainly an influence.  Zodiac was definitely not a sexually sadisitic killer, however. <BR> <BR>Any opinions on this would be nice.  It is obvious he sought out all thin info he could on people who were &#34;like&#34; him---those are his peers.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3503-->
<!--Post: 3510--><!--Time: 1104972093-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3510"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Q<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Q<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 05, 2005 - 4:41 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Is it possible that the mentoring aspect is a Hollywood creation and that BTK and others just refer to other Killers for other reasons?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3510-->
<!--Post: 3526--><!--Time: 1104975988-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3526"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:webmaster@catchbtk.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Tom_voigt<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tom_voigt<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 05, 2005 - 5:46 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->This is getting away from Mike&#39;s profile...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3526-->
<!--Post: 3530--><!--Time: 1104978192-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3530"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Juno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Juno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 05, 2005 - 6:23 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->If Tom will indulge me... <BR>I wasn&#39;t referring to a movie. <BR> <BR>I was talking about his apparent feeling of kinship with other killers, and the fact that he apparently learned from them, albeit through books and, more than likely, experimentation.  It seems clear to me that BTK was well read in the area of serial killers, in particular the sexual variety.  I was thinking of a more...passive...form of mentorship where...he seems to look up to these people and learn what he can from them indirectly. <BR> <BR>Who knows....maybe he wrote Ted a letter.... <BR>Would this fit into a the profile? <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3530-->
<!--Post: 3599--><!--Time: 1105052764-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3599"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Miss<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Miss<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 06, 2005 - 3:06 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->This is my first time posting here, so I hope this is the right place for this.  I just want to say that I don&#39;t think BTK is exceptionally clever or smart.  I think that the serial killers who are never caught like the Zodiac and BTK &#40;at least not yet,&#41;  become like boogeymen to us, because they are unknown.  Because they could be anyone.  But then they turn out to be these little, antisocial losers like Gary Ridgeway, not master criminals.   <BR>Anyway, I think that because he has not been caught yet, it is easy to imagine him as cunning and mysterious and brilliant, but I haven&#39;t seen any evidence of that whatsoever.  I don&#39;t think he&#39;s eluded capture because he&#39;s smart, just lucky.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3599-->
<!--Post: 3600--><!--Time: 1105052935-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3600"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:webmaster@catchbtk.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Tom_voigt<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tom_voigt<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 06, 2005 - 3:08 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Miss, make sure to read <a href="http://www.catchbtk.com/theprofile.html"> <b>Mike Kelleher&#39;s BTK profile</b></a> if you haven&#39;t already.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3600-->
<!--Post: 3613--><!--Time: 1105061845-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3613"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Hbtcontrol<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Hbtcontrol<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 06, 2005 - 5:37 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Mike, <BR> <BR>You&#39;re the expert and although I&#39;ve been following this case for quite a while, and I agree with almost all of your profile, I am actually responding to something you answered in the posts above when you agreed that BTK probably knew one of the Otero&#39;s. <BR> <BR>If we assume that it was Julie that inadvertantly made the initial contact with BTK &#40;and I believe that it was&#41;, he may have been watching or stalking her for days or weeks, or longer. Isn&#39;t it possible, then, that she either suspected or sensed that she was being watched and mentioned it to Joseph?  That would explain why Charlie felt his father knew something was wrong.  <BR> <BR>I also think that in her contact with BTK she gave him her address as part of whatever transaction occured at the time and she may have identified herself as Mrs. Joe Otero or referred to him in that way, so that later, in BTK&#39;s letter, he also referred to him as &#34;Joe&#34; and not Joseph.  <BR> <BR>Does this work? Or are these the type of things that are too detailed and would not be addressed by a profiler?  I am very intrigued by how you, or any profiler, can objectively weed out the unnecessary items to get a good profile.  I get caught up in all the maybe&#39;s, I think.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3613-->
<!--Post: 3634--><!--Time: 1105075946-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3634"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Mike_kelleher<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Mike_kelleher<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 06, 2005 - 9:32 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hbtcontrol &#40;interesting handle&#41;: <BR> <BR>Sure, your scenario could work. However, from my point of view, it involves a few too many assumptions. That isn&#39;t to say that they aren&#39;t well thought out, it&#39;s just to say that from a profiling point of view there is always the danger of making assumptions that can lead in a wrong direction and set an investigation back. On the other hand, if there were some facts to back up your scenario, it could be included in a profile. It is tough and sometimes very frustrating to NOT include assumptions, especially when they seem obvious. Sometimes, as in the case of the Otero/BTK crime, there are sufficient historical precedents to lead one to believe that the first murder victim&#40;s&#41; was not selected at random. That opens the door to making other assumptions, which is fun but can be counter-productive. <BR> <BR>Hope that answers your question. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3634-->
<!--Post: 3945--><!--Time: 1105442917-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3945"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 11, 2005 - 3:28 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Mr. Kelleher, <BR> <BR>In your entire professional career have you so much as <b>once</b> come across a case where a relatively stable, taunting serial killer, who communicated with press and police, <i>deliberately</i> provided damning information in his communiques which led to his capture? Thanks. <BR> <BR>PS: This question is for Mr. Kelleher. I don&#39;t need a paraphrased, cookie-cutter mini profile based on information culled from <i>The Crime Classification Manuel</i> and true crime books as I already know what they say. <BR> <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3945-->
<!--Post: 3977--><!--Time: 1105496367-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3977"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Mike_kelleher<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Mike_kelleher<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 11, 2005 - 6:19 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->George: <BR> <BR>You raise an excellent point. The short answer is &#34;no.&#34; There are cases in which killers taunt with some pretty good information. There are also some individuals out there who subscribe to the theory that many of these killers want to be caught at some deeper level. However, when we use your definition of organized serial killers, they prefer to taunt in a safe manner and definitely do not want to be caught unless something dramatic changes in their lives or they are on the verge of being caught anyway.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3977-->
<!--Post: 3978--><!--Time: 1105497592-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3978"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Q<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Q<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 11, 2005 - 6:39 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The &#34;taunting&#34; in and of itself is a bit of a &#34;they want to be caught at some level&#34; thing if the taunting is with &#34;true&#34; info... is it not. <BR> <BR>But who can say if the info... as with the BTK plethora of info... is true?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3978-->
<!--Post: 3980--><!--Time: 1105498935-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3980"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 11, 2005 - 7:02 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Mr. Kelleher, <BR> <BR>Thank you. And per your initial profile, a dramatic change seems even more likely now and it seems clear that current notes and &#34;drop-offs&#34; from BTK are far more important than his earliest letters in terms of evidentiary value. Thanks again. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3980-->
<!--Post: 3982--><!--Time: 1105499871-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3982"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 11, 2005 - 7:17 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Q, Wanting to be caught -- at some level. That sounds Freudian and old-fashioned but of course I don&#39;t know. With an amateur&#39;s bliss, I tend to be skeptical; after all, it&#39;s been nearly thirty-one years since the Otero attack. That&#39;s a long time for someone who wants to be caught, even at some level. <BR> <BR>One could argue, I suppose, that had the majority of the text of BTK&#39;s letters been provided, sequentially, to the public, as it was received, perhaps he would have been caught a good while back? On the other hand, a lot of people still buy the &#34;monster&#34; gimmick, so who knows?  <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3982-->
<!--Post: 4029--><!--Time: 1105551718-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4029"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Mike_kelleher<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Mike_kelleher<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 12, 2005 - 9:41 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->George: <BR> <BR>Here is what I wrote above: <BR> <BR>&#34;There are also some individuals out there who subscribe to the theory that many of these killers want to be caught at some deeper level.&#34; <BR> <BR>Personally, I have doubts about this theory in most cases. I have seen a few instances in which the wish to be caught was really obvious. In the case of BTK, I don&#39;t sense that same desire. What I do sense -- and what I put in the profile -- is that he has undergone some dramatic life changes of late. Those changes will alter his view of life, his view of himself, and his behavior. Of course, it&#39;s impossible to KNOW what is going on. We can only speculate. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4029-->
<!--Post: 4031--><!--Time: 1105552259-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4031"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Mike_kelleher<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Mike_kelleher<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 12, 2005 - 9:50 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Tom: <BR> <BR>I apologize here for an off-topic message. I just wanted everyone to know that this is the only thread I follow on the MB due to time, etc. I&#39;ve been told that I&#39;m missing questions on other threads. My apologies. If I ever get my act together, I&#39;ll try to make time to look over the other threads.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4031-->
<!--Post: 4032--><!--Time: 1105552987-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4032"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 12, 2005 - 10:03 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Mr. Kelleher, you are right and so is your profile. My speculating about BTK wanting to get caught was too general and not related to your profile. I was &#34;thinking aloud,&#34; which is fine, but not in this thread. I understand, and thank you again.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4032-->
<!--Post: 4089--><!--Time: 1105659768-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4089"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 13, 2005 - 3:42 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Mr Kelleher, <BR> <BR>I agree with your profile that BTK may have attended college at some point but I don&#39;t believe that he has a college degree. I think the stress would have washed him out before graduation. Maybe two years at the most.  <BR>He does have a thing for libraries and books and poetry however and he is organized. <BR>I see him as someone who not only would have frequented libraries but in doing so would bring with a box of index cards that he would catalog favorite books, authors, topics and quotations and paragraphs and lines from favorite books. He would sit a library table with his box of index cards before him and with several cards neatly arranged lying on the table. He would also have at least two notebooks with him and more than one pen or pencil. He would appear to others as someone working on a project or essay or thesis or doing research.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4089-->
<!--Post: 4150--><!--Time: 1105760621-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4150"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Freya<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Freya<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 14, 2005 - 7:43 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Mr. Kelleher, <BR> <BR>Though I didn&#39;t see mention of it in your profile, I was wondering if you might believe that he has some kind of OCD with cleaning and neatness &#40;evidenced by his cleaning up the broken glass in the Wegerle home and complaining about the Otero&#39;s messy car&#41;. I know there are varying levels of OCD, so I don&#39;t really mean that he is extreme, but I wonder if it may have helped him avoid leaving physical evidence on the recent letters. <BR> Assuming that he didn&#39;t, of course. <BR>Maybe I&#39;m reading too much into his behavior.  <BR> <BR>By the way, thank you for providing your expertise. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4150-->
<!--Post: 4151--><!--Time: 1105761047-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4151"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Mike_kelleher<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Mike_kelleher<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 14, 2005 - 7:50 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Freya: <BR> <BR>I see no evidence of OCD. We just don&#39;t know enough, yet.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4151-->
<!--Post: 4155--><!--Time: 1105780722-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4155"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Steve_huff<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Steve_huff<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 15, 2005 - 1:18 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->If there is any ritualistic element - in the sense of he always followed a similar series of steps in the commission of the crimes, not in the &#39;religious sense&#39; - then wouldn&#39;t that indicate a certain level of obsession and compulsion? <BR> <BR>I say that, but I have to put out there the observation that many seem to want to pin him down to one problem - someone wanted to single out narcissism, for instance. Of course he&#39;s narcissistic; most sociopaths are, it&#39;s part of the makeup of that personality.  <BR> <BR>So, maybe there is an element of obsessive-compulsiveness in his behavior. This does not make him an OCD&#39;er. For the record, if there&#39;s a personality type that goes with OCD &#40;the affective disorder, no the personality disorder - there IS a difference&#41; it is often a notably passive and preoccupied personality. Can seem humorless, and may seem to lack insight and empathy, though if you dig deeper, they do have both. I am very close to a classic &#34;hoarding&#34; obsessive compulsive, and they are one of the most gentle and basically sweet people I have ever known.  <BR> <BR>I&#39;d say any OCD seen has more to do with his overall need for control. Manipulation, Domination, Control - these are the serial killer&#39;s usual baseline motives. Looking at BTK from that standpoint eliminates OCD as it is seen in &#39;everyday&#39; people.  <BR> <BR>OCD may be considered in the realm of &#34;normal&#34; psychology. Serial murderers never fall into that realm.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4155-->
<!--Post: 4484--><!--Time: 1106414276-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4484"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Whoisbtk<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Whoisbtk<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 22, 2005 - 9:17 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Mike_Kelleher <BR> <BR>William Eckert was the forensic pathologist who did the Otero autopsies.  He put time of death between 8:15am and 9:00 am. &#40;<a href="http://members.fortunecity.com/ghostiesannex/newsarticles1.html" target=_top>http://members.fortunecity.com/ghostiesannex/newsa rticles1.html</a>&#41;.  <BR> <BR>BTK was seen leaving at 10:35.  Does this strike you as an unusually long time to remain at the scene? <BR> <BR><a href="mailto:whoisbtk@yahoo.com">whoisbtk@yahoo.com</a> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4484-->
<!--Post: 4489--><!--Time: 1106420188-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4489"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Mike_kelleher<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Mike_kelleher<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 22, 2005 - 10:56 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Not necessarily. Some types of killers will often linger at the scene. Sometimes this has a sexual component, sometimes they are collecting trophies, sometimes interacting with the dead victims, posing . . . there are a lot of reasons why they sometimes linger.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4489-->
<!--Post: 4840--><!--Time: 1106769522-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4840"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Featherw<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Featherw<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 26, 2005 - 11:58 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Actually if the pathologist put time of death for the Otero&#39;s at APPROXIMATELY between 8:15 and 9:00 a.m. BTK leaving at about 10:35 would be about right.  Depends on how soon the pathologist got to the Otero bodies to determine the approximate time of death.  If the pathologist was able to examine the bodies within an hour after the murder, his approximation of time of death would be more exact.  But...if the bodies were not examined until hours later, an exact time of death is even harder to pinpoint I would think.  <BR>Thanks. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4840-->
<!--Post: 4878--><!--Time: 1106789269-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4878"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Skov<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Skov<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 26, 2005 - 5:27 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->To Mr MK profiler and all posters <BR> <BR>Just had this idea while going to sleep, so here it is: <BR> <BR>What if BTK has a &#34;higher&#34; common motive with all the killings, a motive &#34;above&#34; the sadistic sexual plessaure he gets from the actual killings? &#40;wich no doubt was a huge part of his killings&#41; <BR>Meaning that the killing of the victim in it self is just the &#34;tool&#34; to fullfill his motive &#40;goal&#41;. <BR> <BR>And that the items he took from the victims was symbols  that in the end would  tell the story of his  &#34;higher&#34; motive. <BR> <BR>Remember he wrote &#34;you guess the victims and the motive&#34; <BR> <BR>SO BTK choose his victims in advance making sure they fit in to the &#34;higher motive story&#34; wich is his REAL obsession/motivation. <BR> <BR>After killing the victims he collect personal items from them in order to bulid a collection that &#34;pictures&#34; &#34;materialize&#34; his higer motive. <BR> <BR>What he is doing now is passing over the &#34;collection&#34; bit by bit, in hope that socity and LE at som point get the message/picture of his &#34;higer motive&#34;. <BR>Try to look at the items as a rebus that can reveal his choice of victims and his &#34;higer  Motive&#34; <BR> <BR>Now lets put the items, he has droped, in a row: <BR> <BR>a watch  <BR>a pearl necklace <BR>a doll &#40;not sure about this&#41; <BR>a bundle of car keys &#40;not sure about this&#41; <BR>an unidentified wrapped metallic object  &#40;Fox package&#41; <BR>poems about fantasies of the victims and the killings of them <BR>Index of a serial killers &#34;story&#34;  <BR>puzzles &#40;words, mathematics?&#41; <BR>Choices of drop off locations might also have a meaning to his &#34;higher motive&#34; <BR>and probably more objects that we havent been informed about yet. <BR> <BR>Besides this he have passed over items that I belive he droped to prove that he indeen was the killer of the victims: <BR>pollaroid pictures of his victims <BR>personal letters to LE, media and intended victims <BR>sketches of the crime sceens <BR>descriptions &#40;in words&#41; of the killings/crime-scenes <BR>Driver licens of victims <BR>several phone calls to media and to LE <BR>and probably more info that we/I don´t know about yet. <BR> <BR>SO IMO maybe BTK´s killings is, in som way, divided in two &#40;probably more&#41; levels/dimensions. <BR>ONE  level is the actual killings and the satisfaction he gets from them. <BR>The other level/dimension is BTK´s &#34;higher motive&#34; which core could be: <BR> &#34;idealistic &#40;philosophical? political? &#40;insane?&#41; fundamentalism&#34; <BR>&#34;religious &#40;insane?&#41; fundamentalisme&#34; <BR>&#34;personal &#40;insane?&#41;family issues&#34; <BR>&#34;occult &#40;insane?&#41; fundamentalistic&#34; <BR>ect ect. <BR> <BR>This could mean that the victims had NO personal  meaning to him AT ALL, insted they were all perfect &#34;bits&#34; and &#34;pices&#34; for the collection that in the end would provide socity with a shocking REVELATION of som sort. <BR> <BR>Please brainstorm on this theorie and add more factual info on the lists. <BR> <BR>I´m completely awear of that I might be totaly off on this, but I choose to share anyway. <BR>And please remeber english is NOT my first language so PLEASE bear over with me. <BR> <BR>thanks...skov<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4878-->
<!--Post: 4914--><!--Time: 1106813469-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4914"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Whoisbtk<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Whoisbtk<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 27, 2005 - 12:11 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Featherw <BR> <BR>One of the fortunate parts of the Otero investigation is the forensic pathologist.  Bill Eckert was recognized internationally for his expertise.   <BR> <BR><a href="mailto:whoisbtk@yahoo.com">whoisbtk@yahoo.com</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4914-->
<!--Post: 5175--><!--Time: 1106937643-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5175"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Devbost<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Devbost<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 28, 2005 - 10:40 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Mike: <BR> <BR>You will find a lot of discussion on these boards that delves into the minutiae of the recent BTK package drops. There is much speculation on the meaning behind particular locations, the packaging, etc. One thread dissects possible anagrams off of the Post Toasties box that contained communication #8. <BR> <BR>My own inclination is to look for meaning in even the most mundane details &#40;and after all, no detail is unimportant if it might help further the work of identifying him&#41;, but part of me also wonders if we aren&#39;t also getting bogged down by looking too hard at details that don&#39;t really have meaning. <BR> <BR>My question to you is: how far into the details is it useful to go before we start chasing shadows? For example, the location of the latest drop probably has some significance, but does it mean anything that he weighted it down with a brick? And the cereal box may or may not mean anything, but does the fact that it was a Post Toasties box and not Corn Flakes or Rice Krispies mean anything? <BR> <BR>&#40;Just for the record, this isn&#39;t a swipe at anyone who is thinking about these things; it just seems to me that a metric for examination is a necessary part of investigating.&#41;<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5175-->
<!--Post: 5198--><!--Time: 1106948327-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5198"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Q<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Q<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 28, 2005 - 1:38 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->In the KSN story {<a href="http://www.ksn.com/news/stories/6880142.html" target=_top>http://www.ksn.com/news/stories/6880142.html</a>} &#40;video too&#41; they mention a post on a BTK message board from Nov. 2004 saying: &#34;&#34;she just started her own cereal killer board. She is posting about Post Toasties right now.&#34; <BR> <BR>Mike do you think this fits his profile... Meaning he is reading these posts and acting on them in some way or do you see this as coincidence.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5198-->
<!--Post: 5219--><!--Time: 1106952422-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5219"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Mike_kelleher<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Mike_kelleher<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 28, 2005 - 2:47 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I think it&#39;s possible that BTK is technologically aware and internet savvy. Personally, I would never discount the possibility that he&#39;s been on this site, poking around.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5219-->
<!--Post: 5949--><!--Time: 1107462366-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5949"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Armchairpi<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Armchairpi<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 03, 2005 - 12:26 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Mike, do you have any input on the <a href="http://www.catchbtk.com/discus/messages/1/414.html?1107461167">BTK Timeline</a>?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5949-->
<!--Post: 5966--><!--Time: 1107469524-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5966"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Mike_kelleher<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Mike_kelleher<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 03, 2005 - 2:25 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Not right now. Too many gaps to make any good observations. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5966-->
<!--Post: 6005--><!--Time: 1107478130-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6005"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lmuncy316<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lmuncy316<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 03, 2005 - 4:48 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Mike, if you profile BTK as going through some type of tragedy &#40;for lack of a better word&#41; and having a military background could the experience have been serving in Vietnam?  Also, what do you think is true and false as far as the clues BTK is giving about himself?  Do you believe his father was in the military, or do you think it is possible he is copycatting Zodiac again?  One of the zodiac suspect&#39;s father was a well decorated Navy man.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6005-->
<!--Post: 6020--><!--Time: 1107481365-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6020"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Mike_kelleher<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Mike_kelleher<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 03, 2005 - 5:42 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I doubt that BTK was in Nam. As to his truthfulness, I&#39;d take most everything he writes with a grain of salt. However, there are those clues and consistencies in his writing that tell us more about him &#40;please don&#39;t ask me anymore on this point right now&#41;. It&#39;s hard to say if his father was in the military but my profile touches on what, I believe, he was like.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6020-->
<!--Post: 6132--><!--Time: 1107544008-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6132"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->One_eyed_jack<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->One_eyed_jack<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 04, 2005 - 11:06 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Mike, <BR>Do you think BTK&#39;s communications coming closer together indicate he is getting caught up in his own notoriety? <BR> <BR>What do you make of him limiting his communications to his local area despite his professed desire to receive national attention? He knows the information will be carefully controlled by the media and the police, yet he doesn&#39;t contact media outside of the area who might reveal more.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6132-->
<!--Post: 6135--><!--Time: 1107544640-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6135"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Scbenson2001<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Scbenson2001<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 04, 2005 - 11:17 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Interesting point, that I think tells us alot about BTK. Despite what he might view himself as, BTK is a hometown boy. I think he would say he was very learned and worldly, but I think the opposite is true. Out of his element, this town where I believe he has lived his whole life, he would feel lost. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6135-->
<!--Post: 6191--><!--Time: 1107570650-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6191"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Mike_kelleher<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Mike_kelleher<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 04, 2005 - 6:30 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Yes, I think the frequency of communications is telling. In fact, his is getting national coverage. CNN did a spot on BTK this evening, during their primetime news. <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6191-->
<!--Post: 6243--><!--Time: 1107629172-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6243"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->One_eyed_jack<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->One_eyed_jack<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 05, 2005 - 10:46 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Thank you for your response, Mike. The local attention has gone national due to interest in the case, but BTK, himself, as far as we know, has not sent any letters beyond his local area. Do you think it is as Schenson2001 has said...BTK&#39;s comfort zone is in Wichita and he would feel uncomfortable communicating outside of there? <BR> <BR>Do you think the notoriety alone would inspire BTK to communicate more or would some kind of increasing stress be a factor as well? There is a great deal of speculation BTK wants to be caught. I don&#39;t think he does, but I&#39;m curious why he is increasing his chances by communicating so often.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6243-->
<!--Post: 7029--><!--Time: 1108140049-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7029"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Neverstop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Neverstop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 11, 2005 - 8:40 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->First time voicing thoughts here - I would think that with the DNA available and the known fact that BTK was comfortable making copies at Wichita State U., law enforcement could easily get a comprehansive list of all male students admitted during the appropriate years. No graduates but admitted students. It&#39;s a time consuming drag but I bet he&#39;s in there. Hopefully this is being/has been done. In addition I believe there&#39;s a good chance he could be smoked out by having the media print deliberate disinformation about him or  some other crime linking  him to it or in some other way push his ego buttons and make him communicate some more. He will be motivated to &#34;correct&#34; the news articles/press conferences. Also, I agree with MISS that this is no genius, just a lucky son of a ----- whose personality isn&#39;t disintegrated enough to lose self control. He&#39;s still in control and having fun but that doesn&#39;t mean he can&#39;t be manipulated quite easily.Lastly, everyone should own up and admit that there IS at least one person out there who knows just who this creep is. Somebody knows that voice and that writing style, authentic or faked, and manipulative pressure through the media needs to be aimed at that person or persons. Case in point, Unabomber&#39;s brother, who really sacrificed a bit of himself by coming forward.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7029-->
<!--Post: 7034--><!--Time: 1108142002-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7034"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Essevi<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Essevi<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 11, 2005 - 9:13 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I&#39;m beginning to believe that he was turned in, interviewed and cleared. He may not fall into any profile. Sure would explain all his self-confidence lately.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7034-->
<!--Post: 7439--><!--Time: 1108497457-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7439"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 15, 2005 - 11:57 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I don&#39;t believe BTK has OCD I believe he knows what he takes to the crime scene and what he takes away, if there is a mess, then he has to be careful not to drop something or leave evidence in the clutter. How come noone has said anything about the fact that these people took self defense classes, where did they take the classes. and Mike have you noticed the pattern of Antisocial behavior disorder in BTK.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7439-->
<!--Post: 7591--><!--Time: 1108590898-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7591"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Wisetherapist<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Wisetherapist<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 16, 2005 - 1:54 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I was trying to find any new information about BTK and found Dr. Schurman-Kauflin&#39;s site &#40;drdsk.com&#41; which has an updated profile.    She thinks that BTK has contacted  jailed serial killers but has not used his real name in these letters.  She also thinks police have his name.  any thoughts? <BR> <BR>Wisetherapist,<a href="http://www.depressionhelpguide.com" target=_top>www.depressionhelpguide.com</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7591-->
<!--Post: 7600--><!--Time: 1108594894-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7600"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:embersageblue@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 16, 2005 - 3:01 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I believe that he has contacted other killers, has to have attention, so comparing notes. and if the police know who he is then why haven&#39;t they arrested him, unless it would be embarrassing, since they have known for awhile from the way it appear, or they could have the same problem we do too many clues to piece them all together.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7600-->
<!--Post: 8771--><!--Time: 1109318297-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8771"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 24, 2005 - 11:58 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Mr Kelleher, <BR> <BR>Your profile mentions BTK as a sociopath who demands attention, and may be a loner. Do you envision a &#34;drug connection&#34; between BTK and his victims &#40;sic.&#41;? I find the drug angle improbable but am happy to be set straight -- by you of course, since this thread deals with your profile only -- by your thoughts.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8771-->
<!--Post: 8794--><!--Time: 1109346992-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8794"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Mike_kelleher<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Mike_kelleher<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 25, 2005 - 7:56 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->No, I don&#39;t see any drug connection in the case.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8794-->
<!--Post: 8796--><!--Time: 1109348030-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8796"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:embersageblue@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 25, 2005 - 8:13 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Mike, <BR>you said in your profile that You believe he works at jobs below his intelligence level, could that be to establish fake identities? <BR>I feel that he was trained in Panama by Joe Otero, todo recon. If that is the case wouldn&#39;t it be possible for him to assume these identities to do hid next job, so to speak. I believe everythin he does has a link to letters, numbers and area flight patterns, Would all these ideas we have about him being a postman, a gas man...just be jobs or ruses for his murders.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8796-->
<!--Post: 8866--><!--Time: 1109368837-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8866"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:whoisbtk@yahoo.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Whoisbtk<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Whoisbtk<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 25, 2005 - 2:00 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Police have a POI in custody, he came from Park City. He&#39;s a Park City Compliance Officer. Search warrant was executed on his house which is near Hedge&#39;s house. <BR>FOX national news supposed to be covering this.  Also America&#39;s Most Wanted is there.  <BR> <BR><a href="mailto:whoisbtk@yahoo.com">whoisbtk@yahoo.com</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8866-->
<!--Post: 8867--><!--Time: 1109368954-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8867"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bodycheck<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bodycheck<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 25, 2005 - 2:02 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hey Who <BR>Btk Media Section... <BR> <BR>Tryin to post as much info as i can find... <BR> <BR>VERY interesting BTK day <BR> <BR>B<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8867-->
<!--Post: 9882--><!--Time: 1109686982-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9882"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Sean<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Sean<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 01, 2005 - 6:23 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Early days yet, but I believe congrats to Mike kelleher are in order. He was certainly in there on many of the points. <BR>Are you happy enough with things Mike? Lessons learned?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9882-->
<!--Post: 9909--><!--Time: 1109700655-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9909"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Mike_kelleher<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Mike_kelleher<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 01, 2005 - 10:10 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->It&#39;s a little early to say, one way or the other. I wish that I had the opportunity to look at the case file. That would have helped a lot. However, you work with what you&#39;ve got. So, we&#39;ll see as more facts about his background come to light. After that, I&#39;ll probably post some observations, etc. and answer your question about lessons learned.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9909-->
<!--Post: 9925--><!--Time: 1109705678-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9925"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Sean<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Sean<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 01, 2005 - 11:34 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Thanks Mike,I&#39;ll look forward to that.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9925-->
<!--Post: 10485--><!--Time: 1109970970-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10485"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:embersageblue@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 04, 2005 - 1:16 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Mike, here is what we have been working on, for Raders background and Possible Vics. I know it&#39;s long sorry , but can you help us fill in any of the blanks Thanks Sheila <BR>2005&#42;  <BR>1/27: WPD recovers BTK&#39;s Post Toasties cereal box communique as a result of letter sent to KAKE tv; the letter indicates yet another communique that WPD has overlooked and quickly locates; both drops are left in rural areas far afield of BTK&#39;s previously understood boundaries; contents not revealed <BR>|- 1/31: Melissa Scott &#40;Valley Center, KS&#41;; c.o.d. unspecified &#40;autopsy results not complete/released; police tight lipped&#41;, children unharmed [more] &#60;<a href="http://www.arkvalleynews.com/web/isite.dll?1107462969820" target=_top>http://www.arkvalleynews.com/web/isite.dll?1107462 969820</a>&#62; <BR>|- 2/3: KAKE tv receives postcard from BTK, it expresses condolensces for the colds 2 news casters suffer, though the rest of the content is not revealed <BR>|- 2/3: KSAS tv receives manilla envelope with undisclosed message and objects. KSAS is a FOX affiliate. [more] &#60;<a href="http://www.kansas.com/mld/kansas/10916990.htm" target=_top>http://www.kansas.com/mld/kansas/10916990.htm</a>&#62; <BR>|- 2/25 - 2/26: WPD arrests Dennis Rader off tip from daughter Kerri, hold press conference declaring they have a DNA match for Rader as BTK <BR>2004&#42;  <BR>3/19: BTK letter received by The Wichita Eagle containing photocopy of photos of the Wegerle crime scene and of Vicki&#39;s driver&#39;s license <BR>|- 4/7: KSN tv receives anonymous letter containing unidentified baby photo &#40;view at catchbtk.com &#60;<a href="http://www.catchbtk.com/16.html" target=_top>http://www.catchbtk.com/16.html</a>&#62;&#41;; presumed to be from BTK <BR>|- 5/5: KAKE tv receives &#34;The BTK Story&#34;, a rambling autobiography patterned after Crime Library&#39;s BTK feature &#60;<a href="http://www.crimelibrary.com/serial_killers/unsolved/btk/index_1.html" target=_top>http://www.crimelibrary.com/serial_killers/unsolve d/btk/index_1.html</a>&#62;, included are two phoney photo ID&#39;s <BR>|- 6/17: WPD receives letter from BTK concerning Otero murders; a second letter is discovered the same day at the Wichita Public Library, contents not revealed <BR>|- 8/17: Jacob Allen; bound to rail road tracks <BR>|- 9/26: Carol Mould; c.o.d. unspecified, arson, items possibly missing from scene <BR>|- 11/30: WPD releases laundry list of clues &#40;view at catchbtk.com &#60;<a href="http://www.catchbtk.com/113004.pdf" target=_top>http://www.catchbtk.com/113004.pdf</a>&#62;&#41; as to BTK&#39;s background and identity, asking for help from the public <BR>|- 12/8: unknown man, presumably BTK, calls quick mart alerting them to package left in Murdock Park; WPD searches park but finds nothing <BR>|- 12/14: citizen finds BTK package in Murdock Park containing Fox&#39;s drivers licence, as well as other unrevealed contents <BR>2002&#42;  <BR>6/4: Dorothy Slaughter beaten, died two weeks later, Mr. Slaughter &#40;survived&#41; beaten, telco cut, car keys stolen, home invasion <BR>2/20: body of Agnes Hayes found near bridge in Harvey County, KS; strangled, police believe crime originated in Wichita or Sedgwick County, known prostitute, body dumped [more] &#60;<a href="http://www.thekansan.com/stories/012805/localnews_0128050047.shtml" target=_top>http://www.thekansan.com/stories/012805/localnews_ 0128050047.shtml</a>&#62; <BR>|- 10/17: Melvin D. Childress; c.o.d. unspecified, body dumped in field, car found abandoned <BR>2001&#42;  <BR>2/20: body of Agnes Hayes found near bridge in Harvey County, KS; strangled, police believe crime originated in Wichita or Sedgwick County, known prostitute, body dumped [more] &#60;<a href="http://www.thekansan.com/stories/012805/localnews_0128050047.shtml" target=_top>http://www.thekansan.com/stories/012805/localnews_ 0128050047.shtml</a>&#62; <BR>|- 10/17: Melvin D. Childress; c.o.d. unspecified, body dumped in field, car found abandoned <BR>1999&#42; <BR>11/12: Tina Frederick; shot in home, blocks from Vians&#39; 8/2004: man incarcerated for another murder charged with Frederick crime <BR>|- 12/15: Opal J. Trumpp; murdered in basement with unspecified weapon, perp. fled on foot <BR>--2000-- <BR>1998&#42; <BR>2/10: Monte E. Dixon; shot in home <BR>|- 2/??: Thomas McCorgary &#40;Harvey County, KS&#41;; convicted murderer was poisoned with Zoloft &amp; morphine, while away from prison in hospital dieing from emphysyma [more] &#60;<a href="http://www.thekansan.com/stories/012805/localnews_0128050047.shtml" target=_top>http://www.thekansan.com/stories/012805/localnews_ 0128050047.shtml</a> <BR>1997&#42; <BR>5/11: Deanna Law found nude in bath tub, strangled, sexual assault, neighbor charged with the crime, but charges dropped despite his confession <BR>|- 6/6: Hattie Smith; strangled/drown <BR>1996&#42; <BR>6/??: Avanthea Williams; c.o.d. unknown, body dumped in abandoned building, known prostitute <BR>|- 9/12: Cherie Fox shot to death, home invasion <BR>| <BR>|- 12/26: JonBenet Ramsey &#40;Boulder, CO&#41;; strangled with garrote in basement, raped, bound, strange &#34;ransom note&#34; letter left in home <BR>Sedgwick County Animal Control advisory board, <BR>1994&#42; <BR>10/29: John Doe &#40;Sedgwick County, KS&#41;; body dumped, c.o.d. unspecified [more] &#60;<a href="http://www.sedgwickcounty.org/sheriff/operations/cold_cases/unknown.html" target=_top>http://www.sedgwickcounty.org/sheriff/operations/c old_cases/unknown.html</a>&#62; <BR>1993&#42; <BR>8/16: Kristi Hatfield found dead; blow to the back of the head, body dumped in field <BR>1991&#42; <BR>1/19: Delores &#34;Dee&#34; Davis abducted from home after dining as same restaurant as Marine Hedge &#40;see 1985&#41;, strangled, dumped body found 13 days later under bridge, bound, telco cut, items missing from home, car wiped down, but apparently not moved &#40;2/26/2005: WPD reclasified Davis as official BTK victim.&#41; <BR>1989&#42; <BR>10/02: Krista Martin beaten to death; blunt object to the back of the head, home invasion <BR>D. Rader worked for US census Bureau, as a field Operations Supervisor <BR>1988&#42; <BR>1/??: Mrs. Phillip &#40;Mary&#41; Fager receives letter from BTK which admires the Fager mass-murder, but denies responsibility <BR>- 9/14: Michael J. Fowler &#40;Sedgwick County, KS&#41;; c.o.d. unspecified, body dumped in rural area <BR>1987&#42; <BR>6/6: Hattie Smith bound, beaten, strangled, drowned in bathtub, home invasion, items missing <BR> 10/31: Shannon Olson, found stabbed following day, hands bound, body dumped in sand pit <BR> approx. 12/30: Phillip Fager, shot; Kelli Fager, nude and strangled: Sherri Fager, strangled, bound; Kelli and Sherri killed in basement hot tub; Bill Butterworth later tried for murders and acquitted <BR>1986&#42; <BR>9/16: Vicki Wegerle &#40;Wichita, KS&#41;, strangled, Wegerle car moved/abandoned, driver&#39;s license missing &#40;photocopy later included in 3/19/2004 BTK communique&#41; <BR>1985&#42; <BR>4/27: Marine Hedge abducted from home after returning from same restaurant as Delores Davis &#40;see 1991&#41;, found 8 days later strangled, body dumped in ditch, telco cut, Hedge car moved/abandoned, ID stolen &#40;2/26/2005: WPD reclassifies Hedge as official BTK victim.&#41; <BR>|- 6/29: Linda Shawn Casey; bound, beaten with &amp; sexual assault with wine bottle, stabbed, home invasion, telco cut, <BR>1984&#42; <BR>Attended reunion of his 8th grade class at RiverSide School <BR>1982&#42; <BR>6/25: Lupe Leo Ornelas; c.o.d. unspecified, body dumped in ditch, car found abandoned <BR>1980&#42; <BR>10/25: Barbara Smith; blow to head, attempted strangulation, arson <BR>1979&#42; <BR>|- 04/28: Anna Williams &#40;Wichita, KS&#41; aborted attack, perp. hid in home awaiting victims, but apparently got bored and left before they returned, telco cut <BR>|- 5/1: Jerry Hunter &#40;Valley Center, KS&#41;; c.o.d. unspecified, car found abandoned <BR>|- 8/15: WPD releases the BTK Nancy Fox phone call to the media and it is heard by the public for the first time <BR>Graduated from Wichita State University Degree in Criminal Justice <BR>1978&#42; <BR>|- 1/31: A &#34;Curley Locks&#34; style poem which refers to the Vian murder, stamped with lettering blocks on an index card, is received by The Wichita Eagle-Beacon, but is initially ignored <BR>|- 2/10: Another letter from BTK is received by KAKE tv; it contains a poem based on &#34;Oh, Death&#34;, demands more media coverage and takes credit for an extra, unattributed, victim &#40;now assumed to be Kathryn Bright&#41; <BR>|- 5/10: Karen, Scott &amp; Mark Pretty &#40;Houston, TX&#41;; strangled/drown, bound with telephone cord, bodies found in bathtubs, car abandoned at nearby apartment complex, home invasion, children murdered ~[more] &#60;&#60;<a href="http://members.tripod.com/bailey_t/index-3.html" target=_top>http://members.tripod.com/bailey_t/index-3.html</a>&#62;&#62; <BR>His daughter is born June 13, 1978. <BR>1977&#42; <BR>03/17: Shirley Vian &#40;Wichita, KS&#41;, bound and strangled with garrote, hooded with plastic bag, children left unharmed, home invasion- perp. knocked &amp; was invited in by children; neighbor boy apparently witnessed BTK knock on door of Vian neighbor &#34;Cheryl&#34;, and saw him proceed on to Vian&#39;s after he got no answer at first home. <BR>|- 6/23: Nina Berardi; shot, telco cut, children unharmed, home invasion <BR>|- 7/11: Sandra K. Talbott &#40;Wichita/El Dorado, KS&#41;; c.o.d. unspecified, body dumped near &#34;Twin Bridges&#34; <BR>|- 11/26: Denise Rathbun last seen; found 2 weeks later; died of drowning and exposure, body dumped in creek under bridge <BR>|- 12/08: Nancy Fox &#40;Wichita, KS&#41; bound and strangled, driver&#39;s license stolen &#40;later contained in BTK 2004 Murdock Park message drop&#41;, home invasion <BR>|- 12/08: BTK calls emergency hotline from payphone to report the Fox murder, a recording &#40;almost certainly edited&#41; of the call &#40;listen at catchbtk.com &#60;<a href="http://www.catchbtk.com/btk.wav" target=_top>http://www.catchbtk.com/btk.wav</a>&#62;&#41; is later released by WPD <BR>1975&#42; <BR>|- 6/9: Carol Marsteller &#40;Sedgwick County/Wichita, KS&#41;; stabbed, body dumped... UPDATE 2/23/05: David Packard convicted &#60;<a href="http://www.dc.state.ks.us/kasper2/offender.asp?id=15497" target=_top>http://www.dc.state.ks.us/kasper2/offender.asp?id= 15497</a>&#62; of Marstellar murder in 3/1987, paroled 3/2004 [more at KAKE tv] &#60;<a href="http://www.kake.com/news/headlines/515277.html" target=_top>http://www.kake.com/news/headlines/515277.html</a>&#62; [more at catchbtk.com] &#60;&#60;<a href="http://www.catchbtk.com/discus/messages/8/85.html?1109184392" target=_top>http://www.catchbtk.com/discus/messages/8/85.html? 1109184392</a>&#62;&#62; <BR>His son is born on July 27, 1975.  <BR>1974&#42; <BR>01/15: Joseph, Julie, Josephine, &amp; Joseph Jr. &#40;Wichita, KS&#41; strangled, telco cut, some bodies hooded, Otero car moved/abandoned, items taken, home invasion, children murdered <BR>|- 1/21: Bruce Douglas &#40;Wichita, KS&#41; body found; asphyxiated and enclosed in trunk of car in rural area N.E. of Wichita, WSU student, car abandoned, car left running, LE ruled &#34;accidental suicide&#34; [more] &#60;<a href="http://forums.prospero.com/n/mb/message.asp?webtag=kr-kansas_news&amp;msg=5105.1" target=_top>http://forums.prospero.com/n/mb/message.asp?webtag =kr-kansas_news&amp;msg=5105.1</a>&#62; <BR>|- 4/4: Kathryn Bright &#40;Wichita, KS&#41; strangled &amp; stabbed to death, Kevin Bright &#40;survived&#41; shot &amp; strangled, home invasion- perp. hid in home awaiting victims&#39; return <BR>|- 10/??: BTK&#39;s first known letter is received- a phone call to The Wichita Eagle-Beacon instructs them to search the Wichita State Univ. Library for a communique, it is found in an engineering book; it takes responsibility for the Otero mass-murder, provides insider-details, and coins the pseudonym &#34;B.T.K.&#34; <BR>|- 11/12: Sherry Baker found stabbed to death, hands tied, home invasion <BR>1973&#42; <BR>11/??: Bruce Douglas &#40;Wichita, KS&#41; went missing; body found 1/21/74 &#40;see 1974&#41; <BR>Worked at Colemans from 6/19/1972- 7/6/1973 <BR>1972&#42; <BR>began working at Colemans on assembly line 6/19/1972 -7/6/1973 <BR>1971&#42; <BR>1/12: Rosy Spencer; strangled, beaten <BR>Rader worked in meat Department At Leekers IGA <BR>1969&#42; <BR>End of four year Stint in US Air Force <BR>1968&#42; <BR>Air Force 1965-69 <BR>1967&#42;-? <BR>10/15: James &amp; Louise Henderson; shot; children left unharmed <BR>1963 D. Rader graduated from Heights High School in Wichita <BR>1940&#39;s lived in Pittsburg Family attended Zion Luthern Church <BR>1965-69 Air Force <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
